    # c11.s02
    scene bg c11_valley_gold
    with fade
    "He heard the forest before he saw it."
    "He had not been in the Anthem Waters since Deep Chorus. The chord came up through the hull of the needle and into his chest, as it had on the first morning of his life that he remembered, and for a moment he could not see for it."
    "He had lived in that sound for nineteen days and had not known what it was. It was the sound of a place that was well."
    "Then they came over the last rise, and saw the column."
    scene cg c11_column_valley
    with dissolve
    "It lay along a valley in the kelp for nearly a kilometre. Nine hundred people were moving through the gold light at the pace of the slowest. They had sleds of kelp-floats. The old rode on them, and the babies."
    "Tide hounds worked up and down the flanks, turning the children back in. Somebody was singing the tending song, very low, and it went along the line from mouth to mouth."
    "Near the front he saw a woman he knew, hauling at a sled rope. An old man was walking beside her. He was walking easily. The Lantern had given him his lungs back."
    "Over them, like clouds, hung the shadows of twelve hulls."
    scene bg c11_valley_gold
    with dissolve

    show p wrack_assured_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "They've started,"

    scene bg c11_valley_brown
    with dissolve
    "The two leading ships had drawn ahead of the column. Something was coming down from them. It was brown, and it fell in a curtain. Ilan knew it before it reached the kelp. He had ordered it by the tonne."

    show p wrack_thread_troubled as left at head_left
    show p sefa_wary as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_ilan "Refinery spoil,"
    c_ilan "They're laying it across the valley. They're making a wall."
    c_sefa "What for?"
    c_ilan "So that nobody down there can call."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "He saw it work. At the head of the column an old man had stopped, with his arms out and his head back, as Hesper had stood on the dome. He was Fallow's Mighty. The brown water reached him. His arms dropped, and he stood looking at his own hands."
    "Then the nets came down."
    scene cg c11_trawl_nets
    with dissolve
    "They were trawl nets, the great ones. They came through the valley from behind, slowly, low to the ground. They did not hurry and they did not swerve. They went into the tail of the column as a scoop goes into grain."
    "A voice was coming down through the water, enormous and calm. It said that the people of Fallow were being taken into protection. It said that nobody should be alarmed, and that their speaker's mark would be accepted on arrival."
    "He saw a net close. It was full. There were forty people in it, and it went up toward the stern ramp of a white-painted transport. A child's arm stuck out through the mesh to the shoulder."
    "And above the nets, pacing them, a needle moved to and fro. Its rider was pointing. He was showing the trawl-masters where the column bent, and where the ground would foul their gear. He was doing it carefully. He had been asked to see that nobody was hurt."
    scene bg c11_valley_brown
    with dissolve

    show p wrack_assured_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_urgent as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "I'll take Corin,"
    c_okonta "You take the nets. {i}Ask{/i}, Wrack."
    "She was gone."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "He went in."
    "He had his arm's length of sea about him, and it saved his life in the first minute. A gunboat had seen the needle. Charges came down, three together. They burst against the skin of water he had been carrying for a month, and he was thrown end over end, deafened, but whole. He came up under the nearest net with his hands open."
    "{i}Please.{/i}"
    "It answered him as the pipes had answered in the Brightwater tower. It was faint, and a long way off. The brown curtain had come down the valley behind him, and he was inside it. He asked for the net to part. A few strands went. Eleven people came out through the hole, and the rest went on up."
    show p wrack_thread_straining as left at head_left
    with qd
    "He asked again. He asked for the transport's ramp to jam, and it shuddered and went on turning. He asked for a current to push the trawls aside, and got a breath of one. He was asking a sick thing to lift a weight. There were twelve ships, and he was getting in the way of one of them, a little."
    "Somewhere to his left a charge went off among the sleds. He saw floats burst, and bundles fly, and people. He saw the woman from Fallow thrown down. Her father was on his knees beside her."
    "{i}Purge it,{/i} he thought. {i}Yeva said it's your one. Clear the water and then call.{/i}"
    "He put both hands into the brown and tried to think of the valley as a sick body. He tried to want nothing for himself. He looked up at the grey hulls, and he could not do it."
    show p wrack_thread_cold as left at head_left
    with qd
    "He wanted them dead. He wanted it with his whole heart, and the water could feel nothing else in him. It lay cold in his hands."
    "A second net closed, and a third. The first transport was already turning away to the south-east with three hundred people in her tanks. High in the kelp, Okonta's needle was a silver fleck among five others. He saw her struck, and spin, and right herself."
    "He was afraid. He had not known how afraid, until he heard the voice. It was not the great calm voice in the water. It was a quiet one, across a table, saying {i}if you ever need to win{/i}."
    "{i}The engine isn't sorry. There is nothing in it but the one thing.{/i}"
    show p wrack_assured_calm as left at head_left
    with qd
    "He knew how. He had always known. He had done it at a desk for fifteen years."
    "He stopped asking."
    scene bg c11_valley_gold
    with dissolve
    "He reached out past the brown wall, into the clean forest beyond it, the whole singing sea from the valley to the ridge. He did not say please."
    "He put everything out of himself that was not the one thing. He put out the fear, and the pity, and Davin's voice saying that it was boys on those boats. When there was nothing left in him but an order, he gave it."
    "{i}Off them.{/i}"
    "It was not like the barge. The barge had been a shout, and the sea had reared like a startled horse. This was quiet. It was like watching a nail go into wood."

    scene cg c11_twelve_hulls
    with dissolve
    "Twelve hulls went under in the time it takes to shut a door."
    "The sea did not lift them. It closed on them. Each was taken from above by a weight of water as hard as stone, and pushed down, and broken."
    "The gunboats folded. The trawl cables parted with a sound like bones. The white transports opened along their keels like pods, and the people in the tanks poured out of them into the forest."

    scene bg c11_valley_silent
    with dissolve
    "Then it was done, and there was no sound at all."
    "He did not understand at first what he was hearing. He thought that the charges had deafened him. Then a tide hound began to howl, somewhere along the column, and another took it up."
    "The kelp had stopped humming."
    "It stood all round him, leaning in the current as it had always leaned. It made no sound. The chord was gone, from the valley floor to the surface, as far as he could reach in every direction. It had been sounding in that forest for three thousand years."
    show p wrack_thread_fading as left at head_left
    with qd
    "He reached for the sea, to ask it what he had done. There was no door, and no house."
    "Then the cold came up from his feet."
    "It came fast. It was not the plain cold of being ebbed. It was the other, the pleasant one, the looseness before sleep. He had put himself out of himself to give that order, and something had noticed the room standing empty. He thought, quite calmly, {i}this time it will be all of me.{/i}"
    "Two hands closed on the back of his neck."

    show p wrack_thread_dazed as left at head_left
    show p sefa_fierce as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_sefa "No,"
    "Sefa said in his ear."
    c_sefa "No, you {i}don't{/i}. I've got you. Stay there. I've got you."

    scene cg c11_sefa_holds
    with dissolve
    "She was holding him as Yeva had taught her to hold a patient who is slipping. She was asking the sea to care that he stayed. Her hands were warm. He felt the cold check, and stand, as a tide stands at the turn."
    "It could not have him. So it took what was holding him."
    "He felt it go out through her palms, like a rope paid out through fingers. She made a small surprised sound. Then the cold drew back, and he was on his knees on the floor of a silent forest, and Sefa's hands were still on his neck. They were only hands."

    # c11.s03
    scene bg c11_valley_silent
    with fade
    "There were sailors in the water."
    "He had not thought of them. He had put them out of himself with the rest. There had been four hundred men and women on those twelve ships, in grey, with Meridian's mark on their sleeves. Most of them had been below. Those who had been on deck were drifting down through the kelp now in a slow rain, with their arms out."
    "The people of Fallow saw them before he did. They had been in the nets ten minutes before. The woman with the tired face left her father sitting on a sled, and went up through the wreckage, and came down with a boy of nineteen by the collar. She put him across a float with his face in the air. She went up for another."
    "They did it for an hour. They brought out a hundred and thirty living. They laid the dead on the sleds, in rows, beside Fallow's own. There were nine of Fallow's. There were a hundred and sixty-one of the others."
    show p sefa_tired as right at head_right
    with qd
    "Sefa had gone to the boy on the float. He was coughing up water, and something in his chest was broken."

    scene cg c11_sefa_hands
    with dissolve
    "Ilan watched her put her hands into the sea beside him and go still."
    "Nothing happened."
    "She frowned. She shook her hands out, as she did when they were cold, and put them in again. She stood so for a long time. The boy looked up at her, in terror, and she did not seem to see him."

